<title>FRANCE: Renault gains against trend.</title>
<headline>Renault gains against trend.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in carmaker Renault rose against the trend on Friday, bolstered by favourable comments put out on the company this week by Salomon Brothers, brokers said.</p>
<p>Renault shares were up 3.09 percent at 153.40 francs at 1400 GMT, while the bourse's CAC-40 index was down more than two percent and PSA Peugeot Citroen was off 1.99 percent.</p>
<p>Salomon Brothers analyst John Lawson switched his rating on Renault's stock to buy from hold. He expressed confidence in its restructuring plans, noted its improved model line-up and said currency movements, notably sterling's rise, were favourable.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
